/-! # MODE-COMMUTE — the FAITHFUL reorder closure and its extract invariance (r19 keystone)

The keystone of the mode-side commutation stack.  The r18 delivery
`arcFaithfulCupCupSuffixExtractCommute` proves ONE adjacent transposition — the cup-cup swap — extract
invariant over the faithful engine `processArcSpineFaithful`.  This file closes that under reflexivity,
symmetry and transitivity: a single equivalence relation `FaithfulReorderEquiv` whose generating steps are
drawn from the shipped commutation arms, and one structural-induction theorem
`extractArc_eq_of_faithfulReorderEquiv` proving the extract-after-suffix read-off is INVARIANT along the
WHOLE closure, not just one step.  This is the standard trace-monoid picture: the reflexive-transitive-
symmetric closure of the independent adjacent transpositions is a congruence, and any observation constant
on each single swap is constant on the whole class (Diekert-Metivier, `Book of Traces`; the dependency-
morphism universal property, Wikipedia `Trace monoid`).  The novelty here is the HETEROGENEOUS witness: the
literal arm carries an on-the-nose `ArcWireState` equality, the partition arm carries an equality-up-to-a-
fresh-block-permutation absorbed by the extract; both feed one invariance theorem.

## The two generating families (K2a) and their arm census (K2b)

The relation is generated by exactly two step families, plus `symm` / `trans`:

  * `ofLiteralSwap` — the LITERAL crossing pairs, each an on-the-nose `ArcWireState` equality, so the extract
    read-off after ANY suffix is `congrArg` (engine-agnostic, NO admissibility).  Covers the five shipped
    literal commutes: cross-cross (`stepCrossArc_disjointCommute`, r10 — the non-allocating r14 class),
    cup-cross / cross-cup / cap-cross / cross-cap (the four r12 hetero `stepCrossArc_step{Cup,Cap}Arc_...`
    literal state equalities).  Smart constructors `faithfulReorder_of{CrossCross,CupCross,CrossCup,CapCross,
    CrossCap}`.
  * `ofCupCupSwap` — the CUP x CUP PARTITION swap, whose two run orders differ FOREVER by the fresh-block
    transposition and are reconciled only up to the partition view; extract invariance is the r18 theorem
    `arcFaithfulCupCupSuffixExtractCommute`, per-step `SpineAdmissibleFaithful rest`.  Smart constructor
    `faithfulReorder_ofCupCup`.

The per-arm single-step extract corollaries `extractArc_eq_ofCrossCrossReorderStep` (literal, near-free) and
`extractArc_eq_ofCupCupReorderStep` (partition, = the r18 delivery recovered through the general closure) make
the K2b census explicit.

## THE CLOSURE THEOREM (K2c)

`extractArc_eq_of_faithfulReorderEquiv` is the closure theorem: any two states related by
`FaithfulReorderEquiv bottomCount rest` extract EQUALLY after the same faithful suffix `rest`.  Structural
induction on the derivation — full four-constructor enumeration, no wildcard; `ofLiteralSwap` via `congrArg`,
`ofCupCupSwap` via the r18 delivery, `symm` / `trans` via `Eq.symm` / `Eq.trans` (the simplest composition
architecture, zero new lemmas, propext-free).  Fired non-vacuously on a MIXED multi-step reorder
(`mixedReorderWitness`: a literal re-expression, the genuine cup-cup renaming, and a second literal
re-expression, composed by `trans`) with a refl-failure probe (`mixedReorder_statesDiffer`: the two endpoint
run states genuinely differ) and a standalone genuine non-reflexive literal witness
(`literalCrossReorder_witness`).

## Honest scope (K3) — what the relation covers vs. the cap exclusion

The generating constructors cover EXACTLY the five literal crossing pairs and the cup-cup partition swap.
The cap-swap PARTITION pairs (cup-cap, cap-cup, cap-cap) have NO constructor — they are EXCLUDED BY
CONSTRUCTION.  This is the r19 conservative scope boundary: the partition arm is anchored on the r18 cup-cup
delivery, and the CAP WALL IS REAL at the root-level renaming vehicle — a cap MERGE flips a merged union-find
root against the join order (`ArcCoreSwapCapFlipRefutation` / the residual (2) renaming witness), machine-
refuted, so `fxMode_hasArcGodementSwapRenameableProof2` stays permanently `false`.  (Note the cap-CROSS and
cross-CAP r12 pairs ARE covered — those are literal-equality hetero pairs with a crossing partner, not the
root-flipping cap-cap merge.)  The keystone marker `fxMode_hasArcFaithfulReorderExtractInvariance` flips
`true` ONLY on the literal delivery of `extractArc_eq_of_faithfulReorderEquiv` at general parameters; it does
NOT build the general-CELL freshness-conditioned partition commute `ArcGodementSamePartitionFresh` that #2043
(WP-AMALG-2 mode-side) consumes, and does NOT construct the root-level renaming witness.  The three permanent
keystones (`fxMode_hasArcPeelGeneralSignature`, `fxMode_hasArcGodementSamePartitionFreshProof`,
`fxMode_hasArcGodementSwapRenameableProof2`) stay `false`, re-asserted by `rfl`.

Raw Lean 4 + Init; structural recursion (induction on the derivation), no `omega` / `simp`-AC /
`WellFounded.fix` / quotients / `propext`.  Strictly ADDITIVE — no shipped r1-r18 file is edited.  Per-
declaration `#assert_no_axioms` AND an independent `#print axioms` gated in the audit twin. -/

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace FX1Poly.Polygraph

/-! ## K2a — the faithful reorder equivalence relation -/

/-- ★ **The faithful reorder closure (K2a).**  The reflexive-symmetric-transitive closure, at a FIXED suffix
`rest` and boundary `bottomCount`, of the adjacent-transposition steps drawn from the shipped commutation
arms.  Two generating families: `ofLiteralSwap` carries any on-the-nose `ArcWireState` equality (the five
literal crossing pairs — cross-cross r10, cup-cross / cross-cup / cap-cross / cross-cap r12 — with NO
admissibility), and `ofCupCupSwap` carries the r18 cup-cup partition swap (its two run orders differing by the
fresh-block transposition, with per-step `SpineAdmissibleFaithful rest`).  `refl` is subsumed by
`ofLiteralSwap rfl`.  The cap-swap PARTITION pairs (cup-cap, cap-cup, cap-cap) have NO constructor — excluded
by construction (the cap wall, honest scope above).  A `Prop` indexed by the two states; a full four-
constructor enumeration keeps the invariance induction propext-free. -/
inductive FaithfulReorderEquiv {signature : ModeSignature}
    {sourceMode targetMode : signature.graph.Mode}
    (bottomCount : Nat) (rest : List (SpineAtom signature sourceMode targetMode)) :
    ArcWireState → ArcWireState → Prop where
  | ofLiteralSwap {stateLeft stateRight : ArcWireState} (stateEq : stateLeft = stateRight) :
      FaithfulReorderEquiv bottomCount rest stateLeft stateRight
  | ofCupCupSwap (state : ArcWireState)
      (fresh : ArcStateFresh state) (forest : isUnionFindForest state.links)
      (nextFreshPos : 0 < state.nextFresh) (boundaryBelowFresh : bottomCount ≤ state.nextFresh)
      (gap positionLow : Nat) (positionBound : gap + positionLow ≤ state.openWires.length)
      (admissible : SpineAdmissibleFaithful rest
        (stepCupArc (stepCupArc state positionLow) (gap + 2 + positionLow))) :
      FaithfulReorderEquiv bottomCount rest
        (stepCupArc (stepCupArc state positionLow) (gap + 2 + positionLow))
        (stepCupArc (stepCupArc state (gap + positionLow)) positionLow)
  | symm {stateLeft stateRight} :
      FaithfulReorderEquiv bottomCount rest stateLeft stateRight →
      FaithfulReorderEquiv bottomCount rest stateRight stateLeft
  | trans {stateLeft stateMid stateRight} :
      FaithfulReorderEquiv bottomCount rest stateLeft stateMid →
      FaithfulReorderEquiv bottomCount rest stateMid stateRight →
      FaithfulReorderEquiv bottomCount rest stateLeft stateRight

/-! ## K2b — the smart constructors (one per covered arm) -/

/-- cross-cross literal reorder step (the non-allocating r14 class, r10 `stepCrossArc_disjointCommute`). -/
theorem faithfulReorder_ofCrossCross {signature : ModeSignature}
    {sourceMode targetMode : signature.graph.Mode}
    (bottomCount : Nat) (rest : List (SpineAtom signature sourceMode targetMode))
    (state : ArcWireState) (leftPivot rightPivot : Nat)
    (disjoint : leftPivot + 2 ≤ rightPivot) (window : rightPivot + 1 < state.openWires.length) :
    FaithfulReorderEquiv bottomCount rest
      (stepCrossArc (stepCrossArc state leftPivot) rightPivot)
      (stepCrossArc (stepCrossArc state rightPivot) leftPivot) :=
  FaithfulReorderEquiv.ofLiteralSwap
    (stepCrossArc_disjointCommute state leftPivot rightPivot disjoint window)

/-- cup-cross literal reorder step (r12 `stepCrossArc_stepCupArc_heteroCommute`, the `+2` offset). -/
theorem faithfulReorder_ofCupCross {signature : ModeSignature}
    {sourceMode targetMode : signature.graph.Mode}
    (bottomCount : Nat) (rest : List (SpineAtom signature sourceMode targetMode))
    (state : ArcWireState) (lowPosition gap : Nat)
    (window : gap + lowPosition + 2 ≤ state.openWires.length) :
    FaithfulReorderEquiv bottomCount rest
      (stepCrossArc (stepCupArc state lowPosition) (gap + 2 + lowPosition))
      (stepCupArc (stepCrossArc state (gap + lowPosition)) lowPosition) :=
  FaithfulReorderEquiv.ofLiteralSwap
    (stepCrossArc_stepCupArc_heteroCommute state lowPosition gap window)

/-- cross-cup literal reorder step (r12 `stepCupArc_stepCrossArc_heteroCommute`, no shift). -/
theorem faithfulReorder_ofCrossCup {signature : ModeSignature}
    {sourceMode targetMode : signature.graph.Mode}
    (bottomCount : Nat) (rest : List (SpineAtom signature sourceMode targetMode))
    (state : ArcWireState) (lowPosition gap : Nat)
    (window : lowPosition + 2 ≤ state.openWires.length) :
    FaithfulReorderEquiv bottomCount rest
      (stepCupArc (stepCrossArc state lowPosition) (gap + 2 + lowPosition))
      (stepCrossArc (stepCupArc state (gap + 2 + lowPosition)) lowPosition) :=
  FaithfulReorderEquiv.ofLiteralSwap
    (stepCupArc_stepCrossArc_heteroCommute state lowPosition gap window)

/-- cap-cross literal reorder step (r12 `stepCrossArc_stepCapArc_heteroCommute`, the `-2` offset).  A
literal-equality hetero pair with a crossing partner — NOT the root-flipping cap-cap merge, so covered. -/
theorem faithfulReorder_ofCapCross {signature : ModeSignature}
    {sourceMode targetMode : signature.graph.Mode}
    (bottomCount : Nat) (rest : List (SpineAtom signature sourceMode targetMode))
    (state : ArcWireState) (lowPosition gap : Nat)
    (crossWindow : gap + 2 + lowPosition + 1 < state.openWires.length) :
    FaithfulReorderEquiv bottomCount rest
      (stepCrossArc (stepCapArc state lowPosition) (gap + lowPosition))
      (stepCapArc (stepCrossArc state (gap + 2 + lowPosition)) lowPosition) :=
  FaithfulReorderEquiv.ofLiteralSwap
    (stepCrossArc_stepCapArc_heteroCommute state lowPosition gap crossWindow)

/-- cross-cap literal reorder step (r12 `stepCapArc_stepCrossArc_heteroCommute`, no shift). -/
theorem faithfulReorder_ofCrossCap {signature : ModeSignature}
    {sourceMode targetMode : signature.graph.Mode}
    (bottomCount : Nat) (rest : List (SpineAtom signature sourceMode targetMode))
    (state : ArcWireState) (lowPosition gap : Nat)
    (swapWindow : lowPosition + 1 < state.openWires.length) :
    FaithfulReorderEquiv bottomCount rest
      (stepCapArc (stepCrossArc state lowPosition) (gap + 2 + lowPosition))
      (stepCrossArc (stepCapArc state (gap + 2 + lowPosition)) lowPosition) :=
  FaithfulReorderEquiv.ofLiteralSwap
    (stepCapArc_stepCrossArc_heteroCommute state lowPosition gap swapWindow)

/-- cup-cup partition reorder step (r18 K1; the ONLY allocating / partition arm — cap-swap partition pairs
have NO smart constructor, excluded by construction). -/
theorem faithfulReorder_ofCupCup {signature : ModeSignature}
    {sourceMode targetMode : signature.graph.Mode}
    (bottomCount : Nat) (rest : List (SpineAtom signature sourceMode targetMode))
    (state : ArcWireState) (fresh : ArcStateFresh state) (forest : isUnionFindForest state.links)
    (nextFreshPos : 0 < state.nextFresh) (boundaryBelowFresh : bottomCount ≤ state.nextFresh)
    (gap positionLow : Nat) (positionBound : gap + positionLow ≤ state.openWires.length)
    (admissible : SpineAdmissibleFaithful rest
      (stepCupArc (stepCupArc state positionLow) (gap + 2 + positionLow))) :
    FaithfulReorderEquiv bottomCount rest
      (stepCupArc (stepCupArc state positionLow) (gap + 2 + positionLow))
      (stepCupArc (stepCupArc state (gap + positionLow)) positionLow) :=
  FaithfulReorderEquiv.ofCupCupSwap state fresh forest nextFreshPos boundaryBelowFresh
    gap positionLow positionBound admissible

/-! ## K2c — THE CLOSURE THEOREM: extract invariance over the full reorder closure -/

/-- ★ **THE CLOSURE THEOREM (K2c).**  Any two states related by `FaithfulReorderEquiv bottomCount rest`
extract to EQUAL `FullArcStructure`s after the SAME admissible faithful suffix `rest`.  Structural induction on
the derivation, full four-constructor enumeration (no wildcard, so propext-free): the `ofLiteralSwap` arm is
`congrArg` off the state equality (the literal crossing pairs, engine-agnostic), the `ofCupCupSwap` arm is the
r18 delivery `arcFaithfulCupCupSuffixExtractCommute` (the partition renaming absorbed by the partition-fold),
and `symm` / `trans` are `Eq.symm` / `Eq.trans` composition — the simplest possible closure architecture,
introducing no new lemma.  This is the observation-invariance-over-the-equivalence-closure of trace theory:
an observation (here `extractArc . (processArcSpineFaithful . rest)`) constant on each independent single swap
is constant on the whole reflexive-symmetric-transitive class. -/
theorem extractArc_eq_of_faithfulReorderEquiv {signature : ModeSignature}
    {sourceMode targetMode : signature.graph.Mode}
    (bottomCount : Nat) (rest : List (SpineAtom signature sourceMode targetMode))
    {stateLeft stateRight : ArcWireState}
    (equiv : FaithfulReorderEquiv bottomCount rest stateLeft stateRight) :
    extractArc bottomCount (processArcSpineFaithful stateLeft rest)
      = extractArc bottomCount (processArcSpineFaithful stateRight rest) := by
  induction equiv with
  | ofLiteralSwap stateEq =>
      exact congrArg
        (fun runState => extractArc bottomCount (processArcSpineFaithful runState rest)) stateEq
  | ofCupCupSwap state fresh forest nextFreshPos boundaryBelowFresh gap positionLow
      positionBound admissible =>
      exact arcFaithfulCupCupSuffixExtractCommute state fresh forest nextFreshPos
        bottomCount boundaryBelowFresh gap positionLow positionBound rest admissible
  | symm _ ih => exact ih.symm
  | trans _ _ ihLeft ihRight => exact ihLeft.trans ihRight

/-! ## K2b (explicit) — the per-arm single-step extract corollaries -/

/-- The per-arm single-step extract invariance for the LITERAL family (cross-cross representative): near-free,
the closure theorem on one `faithfulReorder_ofCrossCross` node (a `congrArg` under the hood). -/
theorem extractArc_eq_ofCrossCrossReorderStep {signature : ModeSignature}
    {sourceMode targetMode : signature.graph.Mode}
    (bottomCount : Nat) (rest : List (SpineAtom signature sourceMode targetMode))
    (state : ArcWireState) (leftPivot rightPivot : Nat)
    (disjoint : leftPivot + 2 ≤ rightPivot) (window : rightPivot + 1 < state.openWires.length) :
    extractArc bottomCount
        (processArcSpineFaithful (stepCrossArc (stepCrossArc state leftPivot) rightPivot) rest)
      = extractArc bottomCount
          (processArcSpineFaithful (stepCrossArc (stepCrossArc state rightPivot) leftPivot) rest) :=
  extractArc_eq_of_faithfulReorderEquiv bottomCount rest
    (faithfulReorder_ofCrossCross bottomCount rest state leftPivot rightPivot disjoint window)

/-- The per-arm single-step extract invariance for the PARTITION family (cup-cup): exactly the r18 delivery
`arcFaithfulCupCupSuffixExtractCommute` recovered THROUGH the general closure theorem — the census entry
"C = the r18 theorem". -/
theorem extractArc_eq_ofCupCupReorderStep {signature : ModeSignature}
    {sourceMode targetMode : signature.graph.Mode}
    (bottomCount : Nat) (rest : List (SpineAtom signature sourceMode targetMode))
    (state : ArcWireState) (fresh : ArcStateFresh state) (forest : isUnionFindForest state.links)
    (nextFreshPos : 0 < state.nextFresh) (boundaryBelowFresh : bottomCount ≤ state.nextFresh)
    (gap positionLow : Nat) (positionBound : gap + positionLow ≤ state.openWires.length)
    (admissible : SpineAdmissibleFaithful rest
      (stepCupArc (stepCupArc state positionLow) (gap + 2 + positionLow))) :
    extractArc bottomCount
        (processArcSpineFaithful
          (stepCupArc (stepCupArc state positionLow) (gap + 2 + positionLow)) rest)
      = extractArc bottomCount
          (processArcSpineFaithful
            (stepCupArc (stepCupArc state (gap + positionLow)) positionLow) rest) :=
  extractArc_eq_of_faithfulReorderEquiv bottomCount rest
    (faithfulReorder_ofCupCup bottomCount rest state fresh forest nextFreshPos
      boundaryBelowFresh gap positionLow positionBound admissible)

/-! ## Non-vacuity — a MIXED multi-step reorder + refl-failure probe -/

/-- ★ **A genuine non-reflexive LITERAL reorder node.**  On the width-6 fresh seed, cross-cross at pivots
`0` and `2` (disjoint `2 <= 2`, window `3 < 6`): the two run orders are syntactically DISTINCT states that the
literal arm identifies — the literal family is inhabited by real crossing transpositions, not only `rfl`. -/
theorem literalCrossReorder_witness :
    FaithfulReorderEquiv (signature := crossModeSignature)
      (sourceMode := CrossMode.dot) (targetMode := CrossMode.dot) 6
      ([] : List (SpineAtom crossModeSignature CrossMode.dot CrossMode.dot))
      (stepCrossArc (stepCrossArc cupCupSuffixProbeSeed 0) 2)
      (stepCrossArc (stepCrossArc cupCupSuffixProbeSeed 2) 0) :=
  faithfulReorder_ofCrossCross 6
    ([] : List (SpineAtom crossModeSignature CrossMode.dot CrossMode.dot))
    cupCupSuffixProbeSeed 0 2 (by decide) (by decide)

/-- ★ **The MIXED multi-step reorder witness.**  A three-node `trans` chain over the width-6 seed with the
crossing-carrying suffix `[crossAtom]`, exercising BOTH generating families: a literal re-expression at the
cup-cup redex (`ofLiteralSwap rfl`), the GENUINE cup-cup partition renaming (`ofCupCupSwap` via
`faithfulReorder_ofCupCup`, whose endpoints differ by the fresh-block transposition), and a second literal
re-expression at the reduct.  Composed with `trans`; the whole is `FaithfulReorderEquiv 6 [crossAtom]` between
the low-first and high-first cup-cup orders. -/
theorem mixedReorderWitness :
    FaithfulReorderEquiv 6 [crossAtom]
      (stepCupArc (stepCupArc cupCupSuffixProbeSeed 0) (2 + 2 + 0))
      (stepCupArc (stepCupArc cupCupSuffixProbeSeed (2 + 0)) 0) :=
  (FaithfulReorderEquiv.ofLiteralSwap rfl).trans
    ((faithfulReorder_ofCupCup 6 [crossAtom] cupCupSuffixProbeSeed (arcStateFresh_initial 6)
        isUnionFindForest_nil (by decide) (by decide) 2 0 (by decide)
        ⟨Or.inr ⟨crossAtom_generatorDom_length, crossAtom_generatorCod_length, by decide⟩, trivial⟩).trans
      (FaithfulReorderEquiv.ofLiteralSwap rfl))

/-- ★ **The closure theorem FIRES on the MIXED reorder.**  The two run orders of the cup-cup swap, related
through the mixed `trans` chain, extract EQUALLY after the crossing-carrying faithful suffix `[crossAtom]` — a
genuine instantiation of `extractArc_eq_of_faithfulReorderEquiv` over a suffix the shipped engine's corrupt box
arm could not carry. -/
theorem mixedReorder_extractEq :
    extractArc 6
        (processArcSpineFaithful
          (stepCupArc (stepCupArc cupCupSuffixProbeSeed 0) (2 + 2 + 0)) [crossAtom])
      = extractArc 6
          (processArcSpineFaithful
            (stepCupArc (stepCupArc cupCupSuffixProbeSeed (2 + 0)) 0) [crossAtom]) :=
  extractArc_eq_of_faithfulReorderEquiv 6 [crossAtom] mixedReorderWitness

/-- ★ **Refl-failure probe: the two run states GENUINELY DIFFER.**  The low-first and high-first cup-cup runs
(after the shared crossing suffix) have DIFFERENT open-wire lists — the fresh-block transposition is a real,
non-identity renaming.  So `mixedReorder_extractEq` is content-bearing: the extract equality is NOT `rfl` on
the states, it is the closure absorbing an actual renaming.  By `decide` on the concrete open-wire lists. -/
theorem mixedReorder_statesDiffer :
    (processArcSpineFaithful
        (stepCupArc (stepCupArc cupCupSuffixProbeSeed 0) (2 + 2 + 0)) [crossAtom]).openWires
      ≠ (processArcSpineFaithful
          (stepCupArc (stepCupArc cupCupSuffixProbeSeed (2 + 0)) 0) [crossAtom]).openWires := by
  decide

/-! ## Honesty marker (K3) + permanent-false pins -/

/-- ★ **Honesty marker — the FAITHFUL reorder-closure extract invariance is SHIPPED.**
`FaithfulReorderEquiv bottomCount rest` is the reflexive-symmetric-transitive closure of the adjacent-
transposition steps drawn from the LITERAL crossing arms (r10 / r12, `ofLiteralSwap`, engine-agnostic
`ArcWireState` equality, no admissibility) and the CUP x CUP PARTITION arm (r18 faithful peel, `ofCupCupSwap`,
per-step `SpineAdmissibleFaithful rest`); `extractArc_eq_of_faithfulReorderEquiv` proves the extract-after-
`rest` INVARIANT along the WHOLE closure over the FAITHFUL engine `processArcSpineFaithful` by structural
induction (`Eq.trans` composition).  Non-vacuous on a MIXED multi-step reorder (`mixedReorderWitness` /
`mixedReorder_extractEq`) with a refl-failure probe (`mixedReorder_statesDiffer`) and a genuine non-reflexive
literal node (`literalCrossReorder_witness`).  HONEST SCOPE: this is the STATE+KIND swap granularity over the
faithful engine.  The generating constructors cover EXACTLY the five literal crossing pairs and the cup-cup
partition swap; the cap-swap PARTITION pairs (cup-cap, cap-cup, cap-cap) have NO constructor — EXCLUDED BY
CONSTRUCTION (the cap wall: a cap merge flips a merged root against the join order, machine-refuted at the
renaming vehicle, residual (2)).  It does NOT build the general-CELL peel `ArcGodementSamePartitionFresh`
(#2043 / WP-AMALG-2 mode-side) nor the renameState renaming witness.  `= true`. -/
def fxMode_hasArcFaithfulReorderExtractInvariance : Bool := true

/-- **Honesty pin — the general-signature peel stays the open keystone.**  The faithful reorder closure does
not build the crossing-inclusive general block-swap witness over arbitrary faithful cells;
`fxMode_hasArcPeelGeneralSignature` stays `false`.  `rfl`. -/
theorem arcFaithfulReorderClosure_generalSignature_stays_false :
    fxMode_hasArcPeelGeneralSignature = false := rfl

/-- **Honesty pin — the #2043 / WP-AMALG fresh-partition keystone is untouched.**  The mode-side general-
signature peel `ArcGodementSamePartitionFresh` lives out of lane; this file does not advance it.
`fxMode_hasArcGodementSamePartitionFreshProof` stays `false`.  `rfl`. -/
theorem arcFaithfulReorderClosure_samePartitionFreshProof_stays_false :
    fxMode_hasArcGodementSamePartitionFreshProof = false := rfl

/-- **Honesty pin — the count-route block-swap / cap-flip witness stays the shared wall.**  The cap-swap
partition pairs excluded by construction are refuted at the root-level renaming vehicle (residual (2));
`fxMode_hasArcGodementSwapRenameableProof2` stays `false`.  `rfl`. -/
theorem arcFaithfulReorderClosure_swapRenameableProof2_stays_false :
